'   the model row ............................ _spec/defs/hermes/hermes-paradigm.puml
'
' ── RULE ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
' On sbx, ANY local model — `--local-model X` or a model-row choice — is served by
' the operator's own Ollama on the host, never inside the VM and never by a server
' proveo starts. The microVM has no GPU on macOS and a passthrough-only GPU on Linux.
' proveo checks, pulls a missing tag, and routes; it never installs, starts or
' tunes Ollama (2026-09-27: pulling added — refusing with `ollama pull` only
' made the operator retype what proveo already knew).
'
' ── NOT CHOSEN: GPU PASSTHROUGH INTO THE VM (2026-09-26, sbx v0.42.1) ───────
' `sbx run --gpu` needs x86_64 Linux with NVIDIA, IOMMU with vfio_pci, and a
' GPU unbound from the host driver (a dedicated card); a hand-built
' nerdbox-nvidia-bundle.erofs, rebuilt on every sbx upgrade; and the
' platform.allowExperimentalFeatures and feature.sandbox-gpu gates. It had an
' open boot failure (docker/sbx-releases#587) and has no macOS path.
' A model baked into the image ran on the VM's CPU (~2 prompt tok/s for 30B),
' so the baked-model images went; one HTTP port to the host's server stayed.
'
' ── NOT CHOSEN: `sbx run --model` ──────────────────────────────────────────
' That mixin only sets *_BASE_URL to host.docker.internal:<port>, dummy API
' keys, SBX_CRED_*_MODE=none, and a network allow for localhost:<port> (read
' from the v0.42.1 binary's embedded template). proveo's own workload carries
' the same env and allow rule (steps 5 and 6 below), so it passes no --model.
'
' ── SEQUENCE (launchSandbox, before the sandbox exists) ─────────────────────
' (selectBackend's sbx branch until 2026-10-16; sbx is now the only backend.)
'   1. GET 127.0.0.1:11434/api/tags. No answer ⇒ refuse with the install URL.
'   2. Tag lookup: exact, or bare name ⇒ ":latest" (Ollama's rule). Missing ⇒
'      size from registry.ollama.ai/v2/<repo>/manifests/<tag> (config + layers;
'      muse-glimmer:30b-mlx = 17.75 GiB), a run-log row if it would not fit in
'      memory right now (memory is transient, the download is not), then POST
'      /api/pull behind a live line on a terminal (one start line on plain
'      output); the start and "pulled <model> (N GiB)" go to the run log, and
'      egress's "local model" fact gains dim "pulled this run · N GiB" (a
'      pull is host preparation, like the add-ons;
'      EnsureHostOllama returns what it pulled). What it pulled is the SUM of
'      each layer's total: /api/pull streams one "pulling <digest>" event set
'      per layer, each with that layer's own total (ollama docs/api.md, Pull
'      a Model, read 2026-11-11). R2 first kept the largest total, which
'      understated a model with more than one large layer (R2 review;
'      TestAPullsSizeAddsUpEveryLayer). The live line still shows the layer
'      in flight. The load check that follows
'      keeps its own ⚠. PROVEO_LOCAL_MODEL_PULL=0 restores the refusal
'      (`ollama pull <tag>` + installed tags of the same repo). A non-library ref
'      (hf.co/…) pulls with no size shown.
'   3. Already in /api/ps ⇒ resident, no new memory, done.
'   4. Fit: need = size + size/8 + 1 GiB against the free memory of the POOL
'      Ollama loads into (FIT POOL below). need > free ⇒ *sbx.NoFitError, a
'      warning, never a refusal (FIT IS A QUESTION below).
'      PROVEO_LOCAL_MODEL_FORCE=1 skips the check. No reading (windows, freebsd) ⇒ pass.
'   5. agent env = sbx.LocalModelEnv(tag) — base http://host.docker.internal:11434
'      — + SBX_CRED_ANTHROPIC_MODE=none + SBX_CRED_OPENAI_MODE=none, the pair sbx's
'      own --model mixin sets so proxy-held auth cannot outrank the local route.
'      (LocalModelEnv moved from the deleted internal/egress, 2026-10-16.)
'   6. Kit network.allow += localhost:11434 — the sbx proxy matches
'      host.docker.internal:<port> as localhost:<port>. Measured: /api/tags and
'      /v1/models both 200 from a guest against Ollama bound to 127.0.0.1.
'      This is an add-on entry; since 2026-10-16 the Kit carries no tier entries
'      (_spec/internal/sbx/policy-baseline.puml).
'   There is no Ollama sidecar any more: the docker plan that could start one is
'   deleted. HISTORY of the sidecar's measurements (GPU loss on macOS, the 32k
'   context floor, one endpoint in three dialects) is below.
'
' ── FIT POOL (2026-10-30) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
' Before: every host measured RAM. A Linux host with 14.6 GiB MemAvailable was
' refused qwen3.8:latest (19.6 GiB need) although Ollama loads it into the GPU.
'   host                         pool             reading
'   darwin/arm64                 unified memory   vm_stat free+inactive+speculative+purgeable
'   darwin/amd64                 RAM              vm_stat (same sum)
'   linux, NVIDIA answers        VRAM             Σ nvidia-smi --query-gpu=memory.free (MiB)
'   linux, discrete amdgpu       VRAM             Σ sysfs mem_info_vram_total − mem_info_vram_used
'   linux, neither               RAM              /proc/meminfo MemAvailable
' Ollama exposes no VRAM endpoint (/api/ps reports loaded models only), so the
' vendor reading is the source. A non-numeric nvidia-smi line ("[N/A]") gives no
' reading and the probe falls through. amdgpu discrete-vs-APU follows Ollama's
' discover/amd.go: mem_info_vram_vendor or board_info ⇒ discrete; else
' vram ≤ 4 GiB ∧ gtt ≥ 8 GiB ∧ gtt ≥ 4·vram ⇒ APU, whose memory is RAM.
' Connector entries (card0-DP-1) are skipped by ^card\d+$.
' Consequence differs by pool: VRAM overflow ⇒ Ollama runs the remaining layers
' on the CPU (slow, no swap); RAM/unified overflow ⇒ the host swaps.
'   https://github.com/ollama/ollama/blob/main/discover/amd.go
'
' ── GPU SHARE (2026-10-30, user: "Split with a GPU estimate") ──────────────
' Measured on a Linux host: RTX 3070 Laptop, 7740 MiB free, only qwen3.8:latest
' (17 GB) installed. "does not fit in VRAM" alone read as "will not use the GPU";
' the operator saw 0% GPU (that run was proveo 218f6bc, so Desktop chatted on its
' host backend and never reached Ollama — not the split).
' A VRAM overflow is a split, so the warning states it:
'   gpu%  = ⌊100 · free / need⌋                     (need = FIT POOL formula)
'   cpu   = need − free                             GiB on the CPU
'   swap  ⇔ RAM read ∧ cpu > MemAvailable            then the CPU share reaches swap
'   qwen3.8:latest on that host ⇒ "~38% on the GPU and the other ~12.0 GiB on the CPU"
'   MEASURED there: Ollama offloaded 19/66 layers, `ollama ps` 68%/32% CPU/GPU — the
'   estimate ran 6 points high; nvidia-smi read ~0% because the GPU waits on the CPU
'   for every token of a dense model (the copy now says so).
' The estimate counts cache headroom on the GPU side the same as weights; Ollama's
' real layer split differs by a few points. RAM rides along with the VRAM reading
' (hostMemory.RAM, NoFitError.RAM); 0 means unread and names no swap.
' Auto-pick (BEST HOST MODEL) still takes only fitting models: a split is the
' operator's explicit --local-model choice, never a default.
'
' ── FIT IS A QUESTION, NOT A REFUSAL (2026-10-30) ─────────────────────────
' memory is transient and the operator knows what else the host is doing.
'   headed (tty in+out, PROVEO_WIZARD on, no PROVEO_SCHEDULE)
'       ⇒ choiceui modal "<tag> does not fit in <pool>", y/N, Enter/esc = stop.
'         stop ⇒ the run ends with the NoFitError text. yes ⇒ ⚠ line, run goes on.
'   headless (schedule, no tty, wizard off, or no screen opens)
'       ⇒ ⚠ line in the run log, run goes on.
' EnsureHostOllama only reports; internal/run decides (admitOversizedModel).
' e2e suites still skip on LocalModelFits: a run that cannot fit is a host
' precondition there, not a harness fault.

' ── CONTEXT FLOOR (2026-10-30, user: "Abide to what hermes needs" → "Derived tag") ─
' hermes refuses tool use under 64,000 tokens (agent/model_metadata.py
' MINIMUM_CONTEXT_LENGTH). It asks Ollama for its window by sending
' extra_body {"options":{"num_ctx":N}} to /v1/chat/completions
' (plugins/model-providers/custom). MEASURED 2026-10-30, Ollama 0.40.13, M4 Pro:
'   /v1 + options.num_ctx 12288            ⇒ /api/ps context_length 32768 (ignored)
'   /v1 + options.num_ctx 65536            ⇒ 32768 (ignored)
'   /api/chat + options.num_ctx 12288      ⇒ 12288 (honoured)
'   /v1 on a tag whose Modelfile sets PARAMETER num_ctx 12288 ⇒ 12288 (honoured)
' The RTX 3070 host showed the cost: `ollama ps` CONTEXT 4096 (Ollama's default
' under 24 GiB of VRAM) while hermes believed 262,144 from /api/show — every
' prompt (~14.6k tokens of system + tools) was cut to 4K and hermes never warned.
' hermes has no native-Ollama provider, so no hermes config reaches num_ctx.
' So proveo serves a derived tag:
'   manifest capabilities.localModel.context: 65536   (hermes; 0 elsewhere)
'   ContextTag(m, ctx)       = withTag(m) + "-ctx<ctx/1024>k"   qwen3.8:latest-ctx64k
'   EnsureContextTag(m, ctx) = POST /api/create {model, from: m, parameters:{num_ctx}}
'       0.1 s, shares m's blobs (no disk), refreshed every run so a re-pulled m carries over.
'   PROVEO_LOCAL_MODEL = the derived tag ⇒ hermes's model.default; hermes's own
'       query_ollama_num_ctx then reads the Modelfile num_ctx (65536) and sizes its
'       compressor to the window Ollama actually serves.
' The fit check counts the window when Ollama's model_info describes attention:
'   kv/token = attn layers × KV heads × (key + value width) × 2 B   (f16)
'     attn layers = ⌊block_count / full_attention_interval⌋ (hybrids), else block_count;
'     a per-layer head_count_kv array sums instead; width = key_length or embedding/heads.
'   need = weights + kv/token · ctx + 1 GiB runtime   (else the old weights + weights/8 + 1 GiB)
'   qwen3.8:latest @64K: 16 × 4 × 512 × 2 = 64 KiB/token ⇒ 4.0 GiB ⇒ need 21.5 GiB
'     check: the RTX 3070 host logged 80 MiB of K+V for its 5 GPU attention layers at 4,096.
'   muse-glimmer @64K: 52 × 2 × 416 × 2 ≈ 84.5 KiB/token ⇒ 5.3 GiB [Inference: no sliding window]
'   MLX tags (qwen3_5) carry no attention metadata ⇒ old headroom estimate.
' A harness whose context fits keeps no prompt; one that does not fit gets the FIT IS A
' QUESTION modal with notes: "<harness> needs a 64K-token context; this run serves it as
' <tag>." and the manifest's rateHint (hermes: Desktop status bar → Tokens per second).
' Auto-pick (BEST HOST MODEL) filters on the same need, so it never picks a model the
' floor pushes off the GPU.

' ── BEST HOST MODEL (2026-10-30, user: "Off + auto-wire best") ─────────────
' hermes ships its own llama.cpp runtime (hermes_cli/local_runtime, backend
' auto = cuda|metal|vulkan|cpu). In the sbx VM it finds no GPU ⇒ CPU; its
' detect.py also skips Ollama by design. So:
'   * entrypoint.sh sets local_runtime.enabled false in the sandbox.
'   * internal/run/local_model_auto.go: a run with no --local-model, no detected
'     provider key, no subscription manifest and PROVEO_LOCAL_MODEL_AUTO not 0
'     takes the first preset in the host's capacity tier that Ollama has
'     installed and that fits the FIT POOL. Below 24 GiB it takes no preset.
'     Only listed models: an arbitrary installed tag (a 0.3 GB fine-tune) is
'     not an agent model.
'     WHERE IT SAYS SO (2026-11-11, _spec/internal/ui/output-vocabulary.puml): the pick, its reason
'     ("no provider key") and the PROVEO_LOCAL_MODEL_AUTO=0 opt-out go to the
'     run log alone (ui.Logf). The screen says it once, as the egress block's
'     "● local model: <served tag> on the host's Ollama (host GPU)" fact,
'     printed after the model is served. Before, the pick printed a ● line
'     under the credentials heading as well (R1 round-2 review). Pinned by
'     internal/run/local_model_auto_test.go
'     TestTheAutoLocalModelsReasonReachesOnlyTheRunLog.
'   * sbx.FittingHostModels does the install + fit filter.

' ── WHY NOT llmman (removed 2026-09-26) ────────────────────────────────────
' sbx bundles llmman, and it served qwen3.8:27b on Metal. It also froze a 48 GB
' M4 Pro: llama-server reserved the model's full 262k context across 4 unified
' slots (n_ctx_slot=262144, n_slots=4), reached 34 GB RSS and filled 21.5 GB of
' swap during hermes's ~14.6k-token first prompt. `llmman serve` exposes no
' context or slot flag. The operator's Ollama had OLLAMA_CONTEXT_LENGTH=131072
' and a VRAM-based default (num_ctx 32768 at 37.4 GiB), i.e. already tuned.
'
' ── MODEL ROW MAPPING ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
'                      darwin/arm64            linux/amd64 (and any other host)
'   Qwen 3.8 27B     → qwen3.8:27b-mlx         qwen3.8:latest       (27b-q4_K_M)
'   Inkling 2 Mini   → inkling-2-mini:26b-a5b-nvfp4   hf.co/unsloth/Inkling-2-Mini-GGUF:UD-Q4_K_M (dormant)
'   Muse Glimmer 30B → muse-glimmer:30b-mlx    muse-glimmer:latest  (30b-q4_K_M)
'   Nemotron 3.5 Super → nemotron-3.5-super:120b-a12b-q4_K_M on both
'   Qwen3.8-Flash-Next → qwen3.8-flash-next:125b-mlx on Apple silicon
'                        qwen3.8-flash-next:125b-a6b-q4_K_M elsewhere
'
' The form offers the first pair (Qwen + Inkling or Glimmer) at 24 ≤ capacity < 96 GiB. At capacity ≥
' 96 GiB it offers the second pair. Capacity is installed VRAM, summed
' across detected cards, or installed unified memory on Apple silicon.
' NVIDIA total rounds to the nearest GiB for driver-reserved memory.
' CPU-only and unknown capacity show no presets. An explicit --local-model
' remains available at every capacity and retains its exact tag
' (2026-11-20, user: "keep current behaviour" for typed and remembered tags below 24 GiB).
'
' ── INTEGRATED GPUS COUNT WHERE OLLAMA LOADS ONTO THEM (2026-11-20) ────────
' user: "make sure M5 is not the only chip with unified memory capabilities,
' AMD has options, research who else"; then picked GB10/Thor, Jetson Orin,
' Strix Halo and the OLLAMA_IGPU_ENABLE opt-in. Apple keeps hw.memsize.
' Rule: count only what Ollama itself loads onto the GPU. Ollama main
' (afc7c060, 2026-11-20) has two rules for every iGPU:
'   discover/runner.go filterIntegratedGPUs drops an iGPU unless it is CUDA,
'   ROCm gfx1151, or OLLAMA_IGPU_ENABLE=1.
'   server/sched.go availableMemoryForGPU caps an iGPU at the host's free RAM.
' capacityFor(linux), first match wins:
'   nvidia-smi total numeric               → that, rounded to the GiB (discrete)
'   amdgpu card, not an APU                → summed mem_info_vram_total (discrete)
'   nvidia-smi prints [N/A] (GB10, Thor)   → /proc/meminfo MemTotal
'   arm64 + /etc/nv_tegra_release (Jetson) → MemTotal
'   amdgpu APU with KFD gfx_target_version 110501 (Strix Halo), or any APU with
'     OLLAMA_IGPU_ENABLE=1                 → min(max(vram_total, gtt_total), MemTotal)
'   vendor 0x8086 with OLLAMA_IGPU_ENABLE=1 → MemTotal [Inference: Vulkan heaps ≈ RAM]
'   else                                   → 0 (Strix Point, Phoenix, Intel, Snapdragon X)
' An APU is Ollama's discover/amd.go classification (no board_info, no
' mem_info_vram_vendor, small VRAM, GTT ≥ 4×VRAM). gfx1151 also counts as an APU at any carve-out.
' The KFD node is matched to the card via drm_render_minor ↔ device/drm/renderD<n>.
' The min() keeps the OS's share honest. With a 96 GiB carve-out on 128 GiB, the OS sees
'   ~31 GiB, and Ollama caps the model there (ollama#16462). Open ollama#19670
'   would lift that cap; revisit the min() if it merges.
' memoryFor(linux) reports Pool "unified memory" with Free = MemAvailable for
'   these hosts, which is Ollama's own iGPU free figure. So the fit question's
'   consequence reads "pushes the host into swap", not a GPU/CPU split.
' Apple stays hw.memsize (user: "Keep hw.memsize"). Ollama's real budget is
'   Metal recommendedMaxWorkingSetSize, measured at 0.78 × hw.memsize on the
'   M4 Pro 48 GB. The launch fit check measures free unified memory anyway.
' https://github.com/ollama/ollama/blob/main/discover/runner.go
' https://github.com/ollama/ollama/blob/main/server/sched.go
' https://github.com/ollama/ollama/blob/main/discover/amd.go
' https://github.com/ollama/ollama/pull/16429
' https://github.com/ollama/ollama/issues/16462
' https://github.com/ollama/ollama/pull/19670
' https://docs.nvidia.com/dgx/dgx-spark/known-issues.html
' https://github.com/mostlygeek/llama-swap/issues/782
' https://forums.developer.nvidia.com/t/gpu-memory-usage-not-visible-in-nvidia-smi/347122
' https://rocm.docs.amd.com/en/latest/reference/system-optimization/rdna3-5.html
' The cache preserves a large model's custom quantization. The registered
' GGUF and MLX presets still map to the current host's build.
'
' Ollama registry manifests (2026-11-18): Nemotron Q4_K_M 90.15 GB, Flash-Next
' MLX 104.85 GB, Flash-Next Q4_K_M 120.06 GB. The fallback weights + 1/8 +
' 1 GiB estimate gives 95.5, 110.9 and 126.8 GiB respectively. Flash-Next's
' hint recommends the 128 GB hardware class. The 96 GB menu threshold
' determines availability. Launch still sizes the chosen tag and context
' against memory free at the time of launch.
' https://ollama.com/library/nemotron-3.5-super/tags
' https://ollama.com/library/qwen3.8-flash-next/tags
' https://huggingface.co/nvidia/NVIDIA-Nemotron-3.5-Super-VL-120B-A12B-NVFP4
' https://huggingface.co/Qwen/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next
' ── OLLAMA FLOOR: INKLING REPLACES GLIMMER WHERE OLLAMA SERVES IT (2026-11-20) ─
' user: "Replace current Glimmer with Inkling Mini 26B"; forks answered:
'   non-Mac → "Inkling everywhere via HF GGUF"; Linux GGUF → "Dormant GGUF, Glimmer now";
'   quant → unsloth UD-Q4_K_M; old Ollama → "offer Glimmer for older ollama versions";
'   verification → "upgrade when stable" (e2e waits for a stable 0.40.17).
' Rule: localModel.floors[platform] is the least host Ollama version
' ("" any, "unreleased" none yet). lineup(tier) keeps, per (tier, column),
' the first localModels entry the host's Ollama serves. Inkling precedes
' Glimmer at localModel.column 2 (grid column 3), so Glimmer is the fallback.
'   floors: darwin/arm64 → 0.40.17 · every other platform → unreleased
'   version: GET /api/version once per process (sbx.HostOllamaVersion);
'            "0.40.17-rc4" counts as 0.40.17; unknown, unparsable or 0.0.0 ⇒ fallback.
'   Ollama 0.40.17 on darwin/arm64  ⇒ API keys | . | Inkling | Qwen 3.8
'   Ollama < 0.40.17, none, Linux   ⇒ API keys | . | Glimmer | Qwen 3.8
' The row draws at most two local models (TWO LOCAL SLOTS in
' _spec/internal/choiceui/wireframe.puml). A typed preset takes its column's slot.
' ""--local-model muse-glimmer:30b-mlx"" on Ollama 0.40.17 reads Glimmer | Qwen 3.8.
' A remembered preset re-resolves to its column's pick (hostTagFor → columnPick),
' and so does a legacy hermes-muse-glimmer variant.
' A typed inkling-2-mini tag on an older Ollama keeps Inkling in its slot. The pull then
' fails with Ollama's own message: the stream's error field carries server/images.go's
' requires check [Inference: streaming error shape, not observed].
' Auto-pick (BEST HOST MODEL) asks FittingHostModels for the lineup's tags only.
' Ollama registry (2026-11-20): latest, 26b-a5b and 26b-a5b-nvfp4 share one config
'   blob — model_format safetensors, requires "0.40.17", renderer/parser inkling2,
'   capabilities completion·vision·tools·thinking; 1250 tensor layers = 18.78 GiB.
'   The tag page labels 26b-a5b-nvfp4 MLX and says "Requires a Mac with 32GB+ memory".
' Ollama v0.40.17 is a pre-release (rc4, 2026-11-10); v0.40.16 is the latest
'   stable. The operator's M4 Pro runs 0.40.16, so it shows Glimmer.
' Linux GGUF is dormant because no Ollama release loads inkling2_loop:
'   Ollama main and v0.40.17-rc4 pin LLAMA_CPP_VERSION b12257, 343 commits behind
'   llama.cpp PR #32694 "Inkling 2 Mini" (merge 29b52d39, 2026-11-20 22:01 UTC).
'   Ollama's own Inkling code is mlxrunner/model/inkling2 (MLX only).
'   Enabling it means setting the "" floor to the first Ollama release whose
'   LLAMA_CPP_VERSION contains 29b52d39.
'   GGUF: ggml-org ships IQ4_NL 16.42 GiB, Q8_0 25.91 GiB, BF16 and no Q4_K_M.
'   unsloth ships UD-Q4_K_M at 15.47 GiB.
' Fit: [Inference] /api/show on a safetensors tag carries no attention metadata
'   (as with the -mlx tags), so the estimate is 18.78 + 18.78/8 + 1 ≈ 22.1 GiB.
'   A per-layer count lands close: 4 global layers (5, 11, 17, 23) with the
'   looped core (layers 6–17, 3 passes) give 8 global applications ×
'   8 KV heads × 256 × 2 B = 32 KiB/token ⇒ 2 GiB at 64K, plus 40 sliding-window
'   applications × 1024 tokens ≈ 160 MiB [Inference: one KV cache per pass].
' Model card: 26.4B total, 3.4B active (5.4B effective with the loop), 1M context,
'   Apache 2.0, released 2026-11-20. Its warning: "less reliable than larger models at
'   following detailed instructions" when using tools.
' https://huggingface.co/thinkingmachines/Inkling-2-Mini
' https://ollama.com/library/inkling-2-mini
' https://github.com/ollama/ollama/releases/tag/v0.40.17-rc4
' https://github.com/ollama/ollama/pull/19799
' https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/pull/32694
' https://huggingface.co/unsloth/Inkling-2-Mini-GGUF
' https://huggingface.co/ggml-org/Inkling-2-Mini-GGUF
'
' The row sets p.LocalModel and nothing else (2026-09-27), so picking an option
' and passing the flag are the same run on either backend.
' MLX on Apple Silicon, measured 2026-09-27 on an M4 Pro 48 GB, Ollama 0.34.4,
' same 2,064-token prompt, num_ctx 8192, one model resident at a time:
'   qwen3.8:latest   (GGUF, llama.cpp)  prefill 103.4 tok/s · generation  9.3 tok/s · 17.7 GB
'   qwen3.8:27b-mlx  (MLX)              prefill 123.1 tok/s · generation 24.2 tok/s · 18.2 GB
' -mlx tags need Ollama's MLX engine (Apple Silicon only); Linux keeps GGUF.
' -nvfp4 is not mapped: [Unverified] which NVIDIA generations Ollama runs it on.
'
' ── NO_PROXY IS A PROXY VARIABLE ───────────────────────────────────────────
' The plan's NO_PROXY (localhost,…,ollama,host.docker.internal) used to cross
' into the sandbox and replace sbx's own, which lists gateway.docker.internal.
' proxyOnlyVar now drops NO_PROXY / no_proxy with the other proxy variables.
'
' ── HISTORY: THE DOCKER-RENDERING LOCAL-MODEL FINDINGS (rehomed 2026-10-16) ─
' MEASURED on the deleted docker+egress rendering; kept because they shaped
' the host-Ollama rule above. Earlier specs said "`--local-model` has no sbx
' equivalent"; that stopped being true when sbx.LocalModelEnv and the host
' Ollama route landed.
'   MACOS LOSES THE GPU IN A SIDECAR. A Linux container cannot reach the Metal
'     GPU, so an in-network Ollama sidecar ran CPU-only and unusably slow; the
'     host's Ollama is GPU-accelerated. That is the rule this file keeps.
'   THE SIDECAR WAS GPU-ACCELERATED ONLY ON LINUX with the NVIDIA container
'     runtime; `--gpus all` was added only when `docker info` listed it.
'   A 32k CONTEXT WINDOW IS A FLOOR. Ollama's 2-4k default truncates tool
'     schemas plus repo context, which breaks every local-capable harness.
'   ONE ENDPOINT, TWO DIALECTS. The env is a superset each harness reads
'     selectively: OpenAI-compatible (OPENAI_BASE_URL …/v1, opencode),
'     Anthropic Messages (ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL, Claude Code). sbx.LocalModelEnv keeps that shape.
'   cursor is vendor-pinned and takes no custom base URL (run.acceptsLocalModel).

actor "Operator" as OP
node "host" as HOST {
  component "proveo run" as RUN
  component "Ollama (operator's)\n127.0.0.1:11434" as OLL
}
node "sbx microVM" as VM {
  component "hermes\nconfig.yaml ← entrypoint.sh" as AG
}

OP --> RUN : model row / --local-model
RUN --> OLL : tags · ps · fit check
RUN --> VM : Kit allow localhost:11434\nenv OLLAMA_API_BASE
AG --> OLL : host.docker.internal:11434/v1

note right of OLL
  **Check and pull, never manage.** proveo
  pulls a missing tag, refuses a missing
  server, and asks before loading a model
  larger than free VRAM/RAM; it never
  starts or configures Ollama.
end note

note right of AG
  **hermes ignores *_BASE_URL.** It reads
  model.base_url from config.yaml, which
  wire_hermes_local_endpoint writes from
  OLLAMA_API_BASE + PROVEO_LOCAL_MODEL.
end note
@enduml
